# What travels with a job snapshot, as an allowlist.
#
# This was a denylist and it missed `infra/.terraform` — 253 MB of downloaded provider
# binaries — so every job uploaded a 265 MB snapshot of which about 2 MB was code. Across a
# fan-out of 55 units that is 14 GB of uploads to ship the same four files, and the state
# file beside those binaries describes the whole resource graph and has no business on a
# compute node.
#
# A denylist was the wrong shape for the same reason it was in `.dockerignore`: it has to
# be right about everything that will ever exist in the repository, and it fails silently
# and expensively when it is wrong. A job needs the package, its metadata and its lock.
# Everything else — the reference clone, the artifacts, the Terraform state, the design
# record behind the `openspec` symlink — is either already in the cache datastore or has no
# reason to leave this machine.
*

!src/
!src/**
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md

# Re-excluded under the allowlist: compiled output is regenerated on the node, and shipping
# bytecode compiled against a different interpreter is a way to get confusing failures.
src/**/__pycache__/
